\f2\b\fs26 \cf2 WHOSE EYES, AND THE TONE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs22 \cf2 \
Interleaved cutaway structure \'97 close-third rotating across Sarah, Eloise, Humble, framed by a concert-narrator layer carrying the High Elvis\'92s speech/song as the connective thread. Comic-satirical register throughout, but the irony (Eloise instantly commodifying an anti-religion anthem; Humble\'92s own flock defecting to the song that will help end him; Sarah privately indicted by a song everyone else takes as pure triumph) should land for the reader without being stated by the narrator or any character \'97 no one on the page \'93gets\'94 the joke. This matches the thematic rhyme already logged for Chanta himself (chanta.md \'a7J: he \'93never recognises his own irony\'94) \'97 the scene\'92s job is to let the reader see what none of the listeners do.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0

