\
LEGAL/RIGHTS FLAG (carry forward, not to solve in drafting)\
The existing \'93Religious Minds\'94 draft lyric (Unused lyrics folder, UUID FCEF04C9) tracks \'93Suspicious Minds\'94 (Mark James, 1968) closely in structure and phrasing \'97 e.g. \'93We can\'92t go on as Elvi / With religious minds\'94 against \'93We can\'92t go on together / with suspicious minds.\'94 This is satire commenting on religion, not on the song itself, which is the weaker fair-use footing. Flag as a known structural clearance question for the publisher\'92s rights team; not a craft problem for the drafter to fix.\
\
OPEN QUESTIONS (surfaced, not resolved here)\
1. Register tension: the brief calls for the speech to \'93echo the register of his inauguration speech,\'94 but the-high-elvis.md\'92s confirmed Close-of-Part-5 note states he \'93stays in his counselling register throughout, never bombast,\'94 explicitly marking the bombastic song-title/call-and-response ceremonial mode as inauguration-only. Recommended reading: echo the inauguration\'92s THEMATIC CONTENT (the One, the One After the One, the Holy Momma) while keeping delivery calm and counselling \'97 but this is a judgement call between two authoritative-seeming sources, flagged rather than silently resolved.\
2. Sarah\'92s exact position during the cutaway: staying on the VIP platform throne established in Scene 2, or physically brought onstage as the Holy Momma per an older author steer (decisions-log \'a7N, verified verbatim: \'93Sarah appears on stage with the High Elvis during his last set \'97 the Elvi demand the Holy Momma be there\'94), which is NOT present in the corrected brief given for this scene. Default assumption here is the platform throne (matches the corrected brief most closely); flag for author confirmation.\
3. Whether the Sages appear anywhere in this scene\'92s crowd shots at all \'97 the brief explicitly asks this be flagged as an open question for the drafter rather than answered here. No content invented for them.\
4. Which pass of \'93Most Have Never Stirred\'94 in UUID 8EF3D700 is the intended final text \'97 the file holds an untitled earlier draft and a titled, more finished draft beneath it. This brief treats the second (titled) pass as presumptive final; flag for author confirmation.\
5. Optional, NOT in the corrected brief: an older steer (decisions-log \'a7N) has the High Elvis call Chanta up for a bow that goes unanswered, \'93and they move on without much concern.\'94 Consistent with canon (Chanta never appears) but not requested in this scene\'92s scope \'97 include only if the author wants it; do not treat as required.\
